My overall conclusion is that we’ve built a sophisticated language for directing and organizing intelligence, but we have not yet established its full performance advantage experimentally.

And that distinction is exciting rather than disappointing: many of the operations are sufficiently specified to attempt real instantiation now.

The next leap isn’t simply another thousand ideas. It’s making a small number of the strongest ideas reliably generate discoveries, actions, and measurable improvements.

That’s when we can start rating the system by what it achieves, not merely by what it understands. 🤜🏻